# Goal Description

The backend currently redirects users to `http://localhost:3000` or serves the old UI (`app/index.html`). The goal is to completely remove the old UI and have the backend (FastAPI on port 8000) directly serve the **new compiled Next.js frontend**. This means when you run the backend, you'll immediately see the new UI without needing a separate frontend server.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> We will configure Next.js to export static files (`output: "export"`). Since Next.js static exports cannot use `rewrites()`, we'll remove the proxy rules in `next.config.mjs`. This is fine because the frontend will be served from the *same port* (8000) as the backend, so API calls to `/api/...` will automatically go to the FastAPI backend.

